    "done_when": "docs/figures/millisecond-converged-solve/diverted-oracle-census/ holds a census receipt JSON beside a regenerated diverted-oracle-census-fine.png drawn through nova.media: draw_nulls gives the read axis a solid triangle, an admitted saddle a filled cross and other qualified nulls hollow markers; draw_wall draws the unit-faithful wall; contours are unfilled lines on stated levels. Every number the caption in docs/evidence/archive/millisecond-converged-solve-landed.html quotes (six coordinates, 26 levels, the psi range) is re-derived from the receipt by named JSON path, and the corrected caption is written to the fragment docs/evidence/fragments/millisecond-converged-solve/msc-diverted-oracle-census-regeneration.html, not into the archive. Open the PNG and state in the manifest which glyphs and wall you see. If the census needs a solve, it runs as ONE H200 job (betelgeuse, reservation gpu_0003_grpA, one card, 8 CPUs, an explicit --mem, TMPDIR=/tmp in submit and payload, the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python without uv, submitted with RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 sbatch, which is a separate job on the H200 node and not a step of the fleet allocation the HOST line describes, and is authorised; never srun or salloc. Submit for real and read squeue after a minute; only if it is still PENDING on a resource or configuration reason resubmit to titan (--partition=titan --gres=gpu:1) and say so; CPU in place on the fleet node is the last rung and its walls are not the GPU measurement, --mem=64G, --time=00:45:00). If the job outlasts your turn, commit, write status waiting with the sacct probe as wait_probe and the job id in wait_condition, and end the turn; the recovery sweep resumes you when the job is terminal. Keep scratch under the run directory, not /tmp, which is at 91 percent on the fleet node; a baseline arm extracts only the subtrees it imports and removes them before the manifest. This gate measures only this node; a failure outside its scope goes under follow_ons.",
